From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:58:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PVE backup: vma reader: detect missing clusters on verify too

The check for clusters that never showed up in the archive only ran
for streams restored to a target, and verify has no targets. So an
archive that ends right at an extent boundary, missing all following
extents, passed verification, while restoring it failed.

Run the check for every stream that is not skipped, on verify too.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Acked-by: Wolfgang Bumiller <w.bumiller@proxmox.com>
---
 vma-reader.c | 20 +++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vma-reader.c b/vma-reader.c
index 1fb6223a5c..d31107a8ca 100644
--- a/vma-reader.c
+++ b/vma-reader.c
@@ -875,21 +875,23 @@ static int vma_reader_restore_full(VmaReader *vmar, int vmstate_fd,
     int i;
     for (i = 1; i < 256; i++) {
         VmaRestoreState *rstate = &vmar->rstate[i];
-        if (!rstate->target) {
-            continue;
+
+        if (rstate->target) {
+            int res = blk_flush(rstate->target);
+            if (res < 0) {
+                error_setg(errp, "vma blk_flush %s failed - %s",
+                           vmar->devinfo[i].devname, g_strerror(-res));
+                return -1;
+            }
         }
 
-        int res = blk_flush(rstate->target);
-        if (res < 0) {
-            error_setg(errp, "vma blk_flush %s failed - %s",
-                       vmar->devinfo[i].devname, g_strerror(-res));
-            return -1;
+        /* verify has no targets, but needs to detect missing clusters too */
+        if (!rstate->bitmap || rstate->skip) {
+            continue;
         }
 
         if (vmar->devinfo[i].size &&
             (strcmp(vmar->devinfo[i].devname, "vmstate") != 0)) {
-            assert(rstate->bitmap);
-
             int64_t cluster_num, end;
 
             end = DIV_ROUND_UP(vmar->devinfo[i].size, VMA_CLUSTER_SIZE);
